{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 34, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Most Wondrous Journey to the Land of the Rising Sun: An Itinerary in the Manner of Master Shakespeare**\n\n**Act I: Scene I – In the Fair City of Tokyo**\n\nUpon the morrow’s dawn when Phoebus first doth kiss the earth with golden beams thou shalt set forth to the great metropolis of Tokyo. First repair unto the sacred halls of Meiji Shrine where the spirits of old Japan do dwell in quiet majesty. There pay homage to the kami and seek their blessings for a journey free of woe.\n\nFrom thence proceed to the bustling thoroughfare of Harajuku where the youth of the land do parade in garb most strange and wondrous. Let thine eyes feast upon the spectacle and perhaps partake of a confection most sweet from the stalls of Takeshita Street.\n\nAs the sun doth dip below the horizon repair to the shores of Tokyo Bay and behold the marvel of Odaiba. Walk the promenade and marvel at the life-sized Unicorn Gundam standing sentinel over the bay. In the evening let thy spirit be lifted by a performance at the Tokyo Bunka Kaikan or by the vibrant lights of the Rainbow Bridge.\n\n**Act II: Scene I – To the Ancient Capital of Kyoto**\n\nUpon the third day take the swift Shinkansen to the venerable city of Kyoto where the ghosts of emperors past do walk. First visit the golden pavilion of Kinkaku-ji where the sun’s rays dance upon the gilded surface and the very air shimmers with holiness.\n\nThen to the bamboo grove of Arashiyama do go and wander through the towering canes that whisper secrets to the wind. Let the path lead thee to the ancient Tenryu-ji Temple where the garden’s stones do tell a tale of zen and tranquility.\n\nWhen the stars begin their nightly vigil repair to Gion where the geisha do glide like phantoms through the lantern-lit lanes. Should fortune favor thee thou mayest spy one of these ethereal beings and catch a glimpse of a world untouched by time.\n\n**Act III: Scene II – Through the Countryside to Nara and Osaka**\n\nOn the morrow’s morn take thy leave of Kyoto and journey to the ancient city of Nara where the first of Japan’s emperors did reign. Here stand the great bronze Buddha of Todai-ji and the sacred deer that roam the temple grounds with gentle grace. Feed them from thine hand and make friends with creatures of the wild.\n\nFrom Nara take the path to Osaka the merchant’s city where the smells of takoyaki and okonomiyaki do fill the air. Scale the mighty Osaka Castle and survey the realm from its lofty heights. In the evening seek out the neon wonder of Dotonbori and let thy taste buds dance with delight.\n\n**Act IV: Scene III – The Final Days in the Land of the Rising Sun**\n\nReturn to Tokyo for thine final days in this fair land. Visit the floating world of Asakusa and the sacred Senso-ji Temple where the thunder gate doth part to reveal a world of wonder. Take a stroll along the Sumida River and perhaps partake of a river cruise beneath the lights of the city.\n\nOn the eve of thy departure take counsel at the Tsukiji Outer Market and partake of the freshest of fish and sea’s bounty. As the sun doth set on thy journey make haste to the tallest tower in Tokyo the Skytree and gaze upon the city that thou hast come to know and love.\n\nWhen the morrow comes and Phoebus arises anew thou shalt bid adieu to this enchanted land. Yet fear not for the memories thou hast made and the tales thou shalt tell shall live on in thy heart until the next grand adventure doth call.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.5009105205535889}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.062493983656167984}, {"token": " Most", "logprob": -0.8476632833480835}, {"token": " W", "logprob": -0.5903459191322327}, {"token": "ond", "logprob": -1.4662635294371285e-05}, {"token": "rous", "logprob": -5.483612312673358e-06}, {"token": " Journey", "logprob": -2.003835678100586}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -0.09428154677152634}